# IEEE 802.3 Manchester encoding of the ASCII bytes of "Hello World!".
# A 1 bit is a low-to-high transition and a 0 bit a high-to-low one; `|`
# marks the end of each byte. Gaps are inserted where consecutive bits
# would otherwise produce no transition, which is why this is a
# self-clocking code and plain NRZ is not.
01 10 01 01 10 01 01 01 | 01 10 10 01 01 10 01 10 | 01 10 10 01 10 10 01 01 | 01 10 10 01 10 10 01 01 | 01 10 10 01 10 10 10 10 | 01 01 10 01 01 01 01 01 | 01 10 01 10 01 10 10 10 | 01 10 10 01 10 10 10 10 | 01 10 10 10 01 01 10 01 | 01 10 10 01 10 10 01 01 | 01 10 10 01 01 10 01 01 | 01 01 10 01 01 01 01 10 |
